<title>GERMANY: Germans seek free market grain export rebates.</title>
<headline>Germans seek free market grain export rebates.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders applied for export restitutions for 5,200 tonnes of free market wheat in a 14.95-24.50 Ecus per tonne range, the state grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They also sought rebates in a 31.0-34.95 Ecus per tonne range for 27,000 tonnes of intended free market rye exports, and rebates of 30.95-34.69 Ecus on 8,000 tonnes of free market barley exports.</p>
<p>--Hanover newsroom, +49-511-36598-11</p>
